###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Force RMSEs are given per element (C and H). The a-C energy RMSE is given as a range (34-36 meV/atom) and the whole CH-QM9 energy RMSE as 'about 3 meV per atom', so neither is encoded. The CH-QM9 role is null because the set mixes training and test data.
# - The SOAP cutoff and sparse-set sizes are in the released potential's metadata, not in the text. Hirshfeld-volume RMSE (0.009 per atom, Fig. 4) belongs to the auxiliary local-property model; dimer interaction energies, defect energetics and applications are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/ibragimova2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

